  "notes": "Long Beach chant-rap, and the research names the arrangement parameter exactly: **repetition count, not chord change**. The hook is the whole song. So harmony is effectively monotonal, the 808 is one distorted note a bar functioning as a *percussion hit* rather than a pitched line, and there are long stretches with no hats at all — snare rolls are the only transition device, which is why this entry’s fill fingerprint is the loudest thing in it. ⚠ `medium`: tempo and key are measured; the drum specifics are partly lane-inherited and the research marks them `[LOW-CONF]`. ⚠ **The countermelody reached 960/1000 distinct answers against a floor of 980**, so its style pool was opened: bell_echo, arp, densityRatio 0.55. ⛔ `counter.rs` reads five styles and this roster only ever authored three — `bell_echo` is a real answer shape the engine can already play and the dataset had never asked for. ⚠ `sustain_pad` is deliberately not added: it is a held pad rather than an answer, and adding one to win a variety score would change what the record sounds like.",
